# autotune-usb-timeout: Auto Tune multimode (issue #205) - the PREVIEW expires
# and the dial stays exactly where it was.
#
# The suggestion is shown ("Auto Tune: suggested +752 Hz - press again") and the
# operator never confirms it. The preview window is 5000 ms from the suggestion
# (not from the trigger), so the fixture advances the virtual clock well past it
# and codifies the only acceptable outcome: the session is over and the dial is
# still on the fixture frequency. There is no auto-apply on expiry and no
# auto-undo either - the assistant simply goes back to IDLE.
#
# It also rules out the opposite failure: a session that never left COLLECT would
# have ended on its own 3000 ms timeout, and one that is still alive after the
# preview window would mean the expiry is not wired.

name autotune-usb-timeout
screen autotune-usb-timeout

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 96000

mode usb
filter_low 0
filter_high 3000
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
